    "result": "I've successfully implemented weekly subscription support for subtrack. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**Core features added:**\n- `subtrack add \"Name\" <price> --every week` to create weekly subscriptions\n- Weekly subscriptions calculate monthly cost as: price \u00d7 52 \u00f7 12, rounded to the nearest cent\n- Weekly charges occur every 7 days from their first charge date\n- Weekly subscriptions appear in all commands: `list`, `total`, `renewals`, and `export`\n\n**Files modified:**\n1. **src/cycles.js** \u2014 Added CYCLE.WEEK, updated MONTHS_PER_CHARGE and monthlyCents to handle weekly with proper rounding\n2. **src/export.js** \u2014 Added weekly to MONTHS mapping and implemented rounding for weekly costs\n3. **src/renewals.js** \u2014 Fixed sorting to use actual dates (inDays) instead of lexicographic label sorting\n4. **bin/subtrack.js** \u2014 Updated CLI to accept `--every week`, updated USAGE text and error messages\n5. **Tests** \u2014 Added comprehensive test coverage for weekly subscriptions across all test files\n\n**Test results:** All 43 tests pass, including 9 new tests for weekly functionality.\n\nThe feature is ready to commit. Would you like me to proceed with creating a git commit?",
